  {
   "id": "eTusmAfNCgAJ",
   "from": "Jonah",
   "author": "fc5d3270037d7478",
   "date": "2015-08-13T16:14:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Reducing the size of a stanfit object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I haven&#39;t tried it, but maybe something like this:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">sub_sample </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> keep_warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  sim </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stanfit@sim<br>  samp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sim$samples<br>  W </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sim$warmup<br>  I </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sim$iter<br>  sel </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">keep_warmup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">((</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">):</span><span style=\"color:#000\">I</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  subsamp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">samp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">chain_samp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">chain_samp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  stanfit@sim$samples </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subsamp<br>  stanfit<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>This doesn&#39;t change any of the metadata and probably needs to be adjusted if you did any thinning, but it&#39;s along the right lines.  </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
